@lessons

Purpose:
  Registry of lessons learned — validated negative knowledge and
  hard-won experience from tasks and projects. Lessons capture what
  worked, what failed, and why, so the AI and humans can avoid repeating
  mistakes. This is the long-term archive tier of the knowledge
  pipeline: deprecated candidates, rejected approaches, stale references,
  and project-specific learnings.

Use this index to check whether an approach has been tried and rejected
before proposing it again.

Owns: ./

Entry Schema:
  Each lesson entry MUST carry the following fields:

  Fields:
    id:             @lesson.<name>
    title:          human-readable summary
    type:           failure | success | stale | deprecated_candidate |
                    rejected_approach | negative_knowledge
    origin:         @task.* / @project.* / @candidate.* / @reference.*
    status:         active | archived
    observed_at:    YYYY-MM-DD
    resolved_at:    YYYY-MM-DD (when the lesson was captured)
    context:
      project:     optional project name
      domain:      optional domain name
      technology:  optional technology stack
    problem:        description of what happened
    why_it_failed:  root cause analysis
    preferred:       [alternative references or approaches that work better]
    references:      [related @reference.* / @candidate.* already deprecated]
    evidence_count:  integer (evidence sources validating this lesson)
    trust:           low | medium | high
    confidence:      low | medium | high

  Example (failure):
    @lesson.no-raw-sql-in-go
      title: Raw SQL strings cause injection and maintenance pain
      type: failure
      origin: @project.payment
      status: active
      observed_at: 2026-03-12
      resolved_at: 2026-03-15
      context:
        project: payment-service
        technology: Go
      problem: Raw SQL string concatenation led to SQL injection
      why_it_failed: No parameterized query enforcement; queries scattered
      preferred:
        - @skill.query-builder
      references: []
      evidence_count: 3
      trust: high
      confidence: high

  Example (success):
    @lesson.payment-idempotency-works
      title: Idempotent command pattern prevented duplicate payments
      type: success
      origin: @task.1044
      status: active
      observed_at: 2026-08-20
      resolved_at: 2026-08-25
      context:
        project: payment-service
      problem: External retries could cause duplicate payment processing
      why_it_failed: N/A (this was a successful application)
      preferred:
        - @skill.idempotent-command
      references: []
      evidence_count: 2
      trust: high
      confidence: high

Rules:
  [L1] Every lesson MUST include a root cause analysis (why_it_failed)
       unless type is success.
  [L2] Lessons MUST be append-only — never modified, only superseded.
  [L3] Failed approaches MUST reference the preferred alternative.
  [L4] Lessons with type.stale or type.deprecated_candidate MUST
       point to their replacement reference.
  [L5] Negative knowledge (lessons) has HIGHER priority than
       positive suggestions — do not retry a rejected approach
       without explicit human override.
  [L6] Expired candidates from candidates/INDEX.sdd are archived here
       with reason.expired_unpromoted.
  [L7] Deprecated references from references/index.sdd are mirrored here
       with reason.replaced_by and a pointer to the successor.
  [L8] Stale references flagged by sdd-knowledge are summarized here
       with reason.stale_review_required.

Integration:
  - candidates/INDEX.sdd → on expiration, archived here.
  - references/index.sdd → on deprecation, mirrored here.
  - REJECTED-APPROACHES.sdd (concepts/) → cross-referenced via
    conflicts_with and related edges.

Navigation:
  Knowledge Lifecycle: @../KNOWLEDGE-LIFECYCLE.sdd
  Knowledge Model: @../concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd
  Candidates: @../candidates/INDEX.sdd
  References: @../../references/INDEX.sdd
  Insights: @../../insights/INDEX.sdd
  RejectedApproaches: @../../concepts/REJECTED-APPROACHES.sdd

State: +
